      {
        "number": 9,
        "internalPageId": null,
        "title": "TO CONSIDER 1. Adjectives are divided into two groups: / Short (1 or 2 syllables) / Long (2 or more syllables). 2. Short adjectives take the –est particles: Joe is the tallest in his family. 3. Long adjectives take the most particle: It is the most expensive restaurant in the city. 4. Short adjectives that finish in –y change to I + est: She is the prettiest at school. 5. There are irregular adjectives: Good – Better than – The Best / Bad – Worse than – The Worst. 6. The superlative for less than is: The least. E.G: That is the least of my worries. 7. ABSOLUTE adjectives do not take superlative level",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "TO CONSIDER 1. Adjectives are divided into two groups: / Short (1 or 2 syllables) / Long (2 or more syllables). 2. Short adjectives take the –est particles: Joe is the tallest in his family. 3. Long adjectives take the most particle: It is the most expensive restaurant in the city. 4. Short adjectives that finish in –y change to I + est: She is the prettiest at school. 5. There are irregular adjectives: Good – Better than – The Best / Bad – Worse than – The Worst. 6. The superlative for less than is: The least. E.G: That is the least of my worries. 7. ABSOLUTE adjectives do not take superlative level"
        ],
